0
00:00:07,412 --> 00:00:09,180
PREVIOUSLY ON
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL,"

1
00:00:09,180 --> 00:00:12,651
THE 14 FINALISTS MOVED INTO
THEIR NEW HOME IN LOS ANGELES.

2
00:00:12,651 --> 00:00:14,486
MADE IT, TIFFANY!

3
00:00:14,486 --> 00:00:15,987
WHEN I GAVE THE GIRLS
THE GIRLS MAKEOVERS,

4
00:00:15,987 --> 00:00:17,723
SOME OF THEM
DEALT WITH THE PAIN,

5
00:00:17,723 --> 00:00:19,891
WHILE KEENYAH AND BRANDY
WERE JUST A PAIN...

6
00:00:19,891 --> 00:00:21,359
I CAN'T SEE MY EYEBROWS.

7
00:00:21,359 --> 00:00:23,962
BUT IN THE END, THE JUDGES
FELT BRITA LACKED THE EDGE

8
00:00:23,962 --> 00:00:26,231
OF A TOP MODEL,
AND SHE WAS SENT HOME.

9
00:00:26,231 --> 00:00:28,100
13 GIRLS REMAIN.

10
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:30,202
WHO WILL BE
ELIMINATED TONIGHT?

11
00:00:30,202 --> 00:00:33,572
♪♪♪

12
00:01:13,278 --> 00:01:16,915
♪♪♪

13
00:01:19,651 --> 00:01:22,187
- TYRA MAIL.
- TYRA WHO?

14
00:01:22,187 --> 00:01:24,389
- TYRA MAIL.
- TYRA WHAT?

15
00:01:24,389 --> 00:01:26,958
- MAIL.
- OH, GOD, TIFFANY.

16
00:01:26,958 --> 00:01:28,527
I'M SLEEPING.

17
00:01:28,527 --> 00:01:29,828
COME ON.

18
00:01:29,828 --> 00:01:33,064
"TODAY YOU'LL BATTLE
TO THE DEATH IN A COLISEUM.

19
00:01:33,064 --> 00:01:34,733
BE READY AT 10 A.M."

20
00:01:34,733 --> 00:01:35,867
WHOA!

21
00:01:35,867 --> 00:01:37,102
ALL OF US GIRLS HAVE BEEN
GETTING ALONG,

22
00:01:37,102 --> 00:01:38,236
JUST HAPPY-GO-LUCKY.

23
00:01:38,236 --> 00:01:39,771
PEOPLE LOOK AT ME LIKE,
"SHE'S TOO SWEET,

24
00:01:39,771 --> 00:01:41,606
SHE'S TOO NICE,"
BUT I WANT TO WIN

25
00:01:41,606 --> 00:01:42,641
THIS COMPETITION.

26
00:01:42,641 --> 00:01:44,543
I'M SURE AS HELL
GONNA GIVE IT MY ALL.

27
00:01:44,543 --> 00:01:46,845
WHY IS THAT UP?

28
00:01:46,845 --> 00:01:47,412
LET ME JUST BRUSH IT.

29
00:01:47,412 --> 00:01:49,915
WHEN I MOVED INTO THE HOUSE,
I WASN'T TOO SURE ABOUT LIVING

30
00:01:49,915 --> 00:01:51,116
WITH OTHER PEOPLE.

31
00:01:51,116 --> 00:01:52,250
IT DOES MAKE ME ANXIOUS.

32
00:01:52,250 --> 00:01:53,285
DON'T CATCH THE EARRING.

33
00:01:53,285 --> 00:01:54,486
I GET PARANOID ABOUT THAT.

34
00:01:54,486 --> 00:01:55,787
IT HURTS YOUR EAR?

35
00:01:55,787 --> 00:01:57,155
NO, I JUST GET PARANOID.

36
00:01:57,155 --> 00:01:58,757
WITH MICHELLE,
THE SMALLEST THINGS

37
00:01:58,757 --> 00:01:59,791
FREAK HER OUT.

38
00:01:59,791 --> 00:02:02,260
MICHELLE GOT PROBLEMS.

39
00:02:02,260 --> 00:02:05,063
TO BE IN THE BOTTOM TWO
DOES NOT FEEL GOOD AT ALL.

40
00:02:05,063 --> 00:02:07,833
TYRA, SHE WAS TALKING
ABOUT MY ATTITUDE.

41
00:02:07,833 --> 00:02:08,834
HOW ARE YOU SLEEPIN'?

42
00:02:08,834 --> 00:02:10,869
'CAUSE Y'ALL ARE TAKING LONG.

43
00:02:10,869 --> 00:02:15,540
I THINK MY GREATEST OPPONENT
RIGHT NOW IS MYSELF.

44
00:02:17,576 --> 00:02:19,711
TYRA MAIL SAID IT WOULD BE
A FIGHT TO THE DEATH

45
00:02:19,711 --> 00:02:21,079
IN THE COLISEUM.

46
00:02:21,079 --> 00:02:23,081
MAYBE WE'RE GONNA BE
DRESSED LIKE GLADIATORS.

47
00:02:23,081 --> 00:02:24,816
WE ARE SUCH SPECULATORS,
WE'RE HORRIBLE.

48
00:02:24,816 --> 00:02:25,817
WHAT THE HECK?

49
00:02:25,817 --> 00:02:26,885
CHEERLEADERS.

50
00:02:26,885 --> 00:02:29,521
OH, MY GOD.

51
00:02:29,521 --> 00:02:30,989
I WAS LIKE WHAT?

52
00:02:30,989 --> 00:02:32,190
I HATE CHEERLEADERS.

53
00:02:32,190 --> 00:02:33,658
THAT'S ALL WE NEED
IS THREE MORE PRETTY GIRLS

54
00:02:33,658 --> 00:02:36,862
TO ADD TO THE COLLECTION.

55
00:02:36,862 --> 00:02:39,397
(cheers and applause)

56
00:02:39,397 --> 00:02:43,635
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL."

57
00:02:43,635 --> 00:02:45,770
YAY!

58
00:02:45,770 --> 00:02:47,205
MISS J. WEARING
A CHEERLEADING OUTFIT

59
00:02:47,205 --> 00:02:49,007
AND POM-POMS IN HIS HAIR
AND PIGTAILS.

60
00:02:49,007 --> 00:02:52,143
HE LOOKED
REALLY CUTE, ACTUALLY.

61
00:02:52,143 --> 00:02:54,913
MISS J. IS INVOLVED,
YOU KNOW THERE'S GONNA BE

62
00:02:54,913 --> 00:02:55,981
WALKING INVOLVED.

63
00:02:55,981 --> 00:02:57,215
GIRLS, YOU'RE HERE
FOR A CRASH COURSE

64
00:02:57,215 --> 00:02:58,817
OF MISS J.'s RUNWAY TEACH.

65
00:02:58,817 --> 00:03:00,986
HERE ARE PAIRS
OF PLATFORM CLOGS.

66
00:03:00,986 --> 00:03:02,988
SO GRAB A PAIR AND MEET ME
ON THE FIELD, OKAY?

67
00:03:02,988 --> 00:03:06,458
WORK IT OUT.

68
00:03:06,458 --> 00:03:09,127
I JUST SAW A SHOW RECENTLY
WHERE A DESIGNER HAD THE GIRLS

69
00:03:09,127 --> 00:03:10,795
WALKING IN A GARDEN.

70
00:03:10,795 --> 00:03:14,299
THIS IS VERY, VERY DIFFICULT,
TO GET A GIRL WALKING ON GRASS

71
00:03:14,299 --> 00:03:15,300
AND FEEL COMFORTABLE.

72
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:16,334
BAM.

73
00:03:16,334 --> 00:03:17,335
THE GIRLS NEED TO HAVE
A PRESENCE.

74
00:03:17,335 --> 00:03:18,803
HIT IT.

75
00:03:18,803 --> 00:03:20,238
HEADS UP, TIFFANY,
HEADS UP.

76
00:03:20,238 --> 00:03:21,239
I KNOW I'M GONNA FALL.

77
00:03:21,239 --> 00:03:22,474
LOOK STRAIGHT AHEAD.

78
00:03:22,474 --> 00:03:24,576
IT'S NOT EASY
WALKING ON GRASS, IS IT?

79
00:03:24,576 --> 00:03:27,112
THERE'S A TRICK, AND THAT IS
TRY NOT TO MODEL.

80
00:03:27,112 --> 00:03:28,213
PRESENCE.

81
00:03:28,213 --> 00:03:32,918
♪♪♪

82
00:03:32,918 --> 00:03:34,452
MICHELLE, YOU WALK LIKE

83
00:03:34,452 --> 00:03:38,390
YOU HAVE SPINA BIFIDA
ON THE RIGHT SIDE OF YOUR BODY.

84
00:03:38,390 --> 00:03:40,825
I KNOW YOU'RE TRYING TO KEEP UP,
BUT RELAX IT.

85
00:03:40,825 --> 00:03:45,096
MICHELLE WALKS AS THOUGH SHE
HAS THE WORLD ON HER SHOULDERS.

86
00:03:45,096 --> 00:03:46,898
KAHLEN, GET THE SHOULDER BACK
A BIT, BABY.

87
00:03:46,898 --> 00:03:52,904
IF YOU DON'T PULL YOUR HEAD UP,
YOU'RE LIKE A MELTED CANDLE.

88
00:03:52,904 --> 00:03:55,140
BRANDY, YOU'RE WALKING
A BIT LIKE THIS.

89
00:03:55,140 --> 00:03:59,577
LEADING WITH HER CHIN,
THAT NEEDS TO BE CORRECTED.

90
00:03:59,577 --> 00:04:04,716
NOT BAD, LLUVY,
NOT BAD, NOT BAD, NOT BAD.

91
00:04:04,716 --> 00:04:07,819
TATIANA--
GIRL, TAKE LONGER STEPS.

92
00:04:07,819 --> 00:04:13,758
SARAH, PICK IT UP.

93
00:04:13,758 --> 00:04:16,027
SARAH WAS WALKING
QUITE HEAVY-FOOTED.

94
00:04:16,027 --> 00:04:17,362
YOU SAY IT'S YOUR SHOE?

95
00:04:17,362 --> 00:04:18,496
OKAY.

96
00:04:18,496 --> 00:04:22,634
WALKING ON GRASS IN BIG,
CHUNKY BLACK CLOG SHOES,

97
00:04:22,634 --> 00:04:24,302
IT DIDN'T GO SO GOOD FOR ME.

98
00:04:24,302 --> 00:04:27,004
MISS FASHION VICTIM, I WANT
YOU TO BE ONE OF THE GOD'S

99
00:04:27,004 --> 00:04:28,707
EXTRA SPECIAL CHILDREN

100
00:04:28,707 --> 00:04:32,377
'CAUSE YOU NEED
THE HELP.

101
00:04:32,377 --> 00:04:36,114
SOMEWHERE IN THIS
WONDERFUL STADIUM

102
00:04:36,114 --> 00:04:39,985
IS A PAIR OF HIGH HEELS
FOR EACH AND EVERY ONE OF YOU.

103
00:04:39,985 --> 00:04:41,286
ALL UP HERE?

104
00:04:41,286 --> 00:04:42,287
THE STADIUM WAS HUGE.

105
00:04:42,287 --> 00:04:44,422
I MEAN, ABSOLUTELY HUGE!

106
00:04:44,422 --> 00:04:48,059
I NEED YOU TO HAVE
THOSE SHOES IN YOUR HAND

107
00:04:48,059 --> 00:04:49,361
AND THEN ON YOUR FEET.

108
00:04:49,361 --> 00:04:51,096
ON THE COUNT OF THREE.

109
00:04:51,096 --> 00:04:53,798
ONE, TWO, THREE!

110
00:04:53,798 --> 00:04:56,901
♪♪♪

111
00:04:56,901 --> 00:04:58,036
SCAVENGER HUNT,

112
00:04:58,036 --> 00:05:03,174
SCAVENGER
HUNT, SCAVENGER HUNT.

113
00:05:03,174 --> 00:05:04,542
I DON'T SEE ANY SHOES!

114
00:05:04,542 --> 00:05:06,144
WHERE THE... ARE THEY?

115
00:05:06,144 --> 00:05:07,312
WE DON'T SEE ANY SHOES.

116
00:05:07,312 --> 00:05:08,713
WE DON'T SEE ANY SHOES,
WHERE ARE THE SHOES?

117
00:05:08,713 --> 00:05:09,981
OH, MY GOSH,
WHERE ARE THE SHOES.

118
00:05:09,981 --> 00:05:12,751
I JUST LOOK UP, AND I SEE
ALL 13 PAIRS OF SHOES.

119
00:05:12,751 --> 00:05:15,987
WHEN I CALL YOUR A NAME,
YOU'LL BE GIVEN AN ACCESSORY.

120
00:05:15,987 --> 00:05:18,523
THE MOST DIFFICULT THING
FOR A GIRL TO UNDERSTAND

121
00:05:18,523 --> 00:05:21,026
IS THAT YOU NEED TO GO OUT THERE
AND REALLY PRESENT THE CLOTHES

122
00:05:21,026 --> 00:05:22,594
IN DIFFERENT SITUATIONS.

123
00:05:22,594 --> 00:05:25,196
THE KEY TO WALKING WITH
A REALLY HUGE ACCESSORY

124
00:05:25,196 --> 00:05:27,165
IS TO GIVE IT YOUR BEST SHOT,
BUT NOT NECESSARILY TO GIVE

125
00:05:27,165 --> 00:05:29,300
THAT OVER-THE-TOP
RUNWAY STOMP.

126
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:31,503
AND IT'S ALWAYS A SURPRISE
WHEN GIRLS HAVE TO WALK

127
00:05:31,503 --> 00:05:32,737
DOWN STEPS.

128
00:05:32,737 --> 00:05:34,973
AND I'M GONNA DEMONSTRATE
HOW IT CAN BE DONE.

129
00:05:34,973 --> 00:05:36,441
SO THESE ARE MY ACCESSORIES.

130
00:05:36,441 --> 00:05:38,276
YOU KNOW,
I MAY WALK LIKE THIS.

131
00:05:38,276 --> 00:05:39,878
♪♪♪

132
00:05:48,420 --> 00:05:50,555
YOU GUYS ARE OKAY.

133
00:05:50,555 --> 00:05:51,689
MISS BRANDY.

134
00:05:51,689 --> 00:05:54,259
- OH, SHOOT.
- UH-HUH.

135
00:05:54,259 --> 00:05:56,061
YOU LOOK LIKE YOU'RE ABOUT
TO BE TIED AND BEAT.

136
00:05:56,061 --> 00:05:58,897
YEAH.

137
00:06:06,271 --> 00:06:08,940
I FEEL LIKE I'M AT THE RACES
WITH THE TORTOISE AND THE HARE

138
00:06:08,940 --> 00:06:11,242
AND, SARAH,
THAT YOU'RE THE TORTOISE.

139
00:06:11,242 --> 00:06:14,879
BECKY!

140
00:06:14,879 --> 00:06:16,815
RUNWAY IS MY FAVORITE PART
OF MODELING.

141
00:06:16,815 --> 00:06:18,983
I'VE NEVER REALLY HAD
FORMAL TRAINING,

142
00:06:18,983 --> 00:06:21,052
BUT I DO STILL FEEL CONFIDENT
IN RUNWAY,

143
00:06:21,052 --> 00:06:22,720
SO I REALLY DON'T KNOW
WHAT THE BEST RUNWAY COACH

144
00:06:22,720 --> 00:06:24,222
IN THE WORLD
IS GONNA TELL ME.

145
00:06:24,222 --> 00:06:25,824
I THINK BECKY FEELS
QUITE CONFIDENT

146
00:06:25,824 --> 00:06:26,825
WITH A LOT
OF HAIR ON HER HEAD.

147
00:06:26,825 --> 00:06:30,628
♪♪♪

148
00:06:36,901 --> 00:06:38,970
OKAY, GIRL,
STILL WITH ELEGANCE.

149
00:06:38,970 --> 00:06:41,372
BRITTANY REMINDS ME
OF JANICE DICKINSON.

150
00:06:41,372 --> 00:06:43,041
SHE NEEDS TO BRING IT DOWN
A LEVEL.

151
00:06:43,041 --> 00:06:46,511
J. SAID THAT I'M TOO SEXY,
I NEED TO TONE IT DOWN.

152
00:06:46,511 --> 00:06:48,346
WHICH IS NICE,
AT LEAST IT'S NOT,

153
00:06:48,346 --> 00:06:51,382
"YOU'RE VERY AWKWARD."

154
00:06:51,382 --> 00:06:52,684
OKAY, GIRLS,
SO THANK YOU VERY MUCH

155
00:06:52,684 --> 00:06:54,185
FOR YOUR TIME AND PATIENCE.

156
00:06:54,185 --> 00:06:58,022
SOMETIMES YOU HAVE TO WALK
ON GRASS, PEBBLES, STEPS.

157
00:06:58,022 --> 00:07:01,159
WHEN YOU HAVE TO WALK ON THINGS
LIKE THAT, TRY TO HAVE PRESENCE.

158
00:07:01,159 --> 00:07:02,494
THANK YOU.

159
00:07:02,494 --> 00:07:03,628
SEE YOU GIRLS LATER, OKAY?

160
00:07:03,628 --> 00:07:05,964
BRAVO.

161
00:07:05,964 --> 00:07:09,634
♪♪♪

162
00:07:09,634 --> 00:07:11,035
DON'T FORGET THE FIRST DRILL

163
00:07:11,035 --> 00:07:14,205
THAT J. TAUGHT US WAS WALKING
IN A STRAIGHT LINE.

164
00:07:14,205 --> 00:07:17,609
I LEFT THE COLISEUM FEELING
A LITTLE BAD ABOUT MY WALK.

165
00:07:17,609 --> 00:07:20,011
KEENYAH HAS A VERY GOOD WALK,
SO I ASKED HER

166
00:07:20,011 --> 00:07:21,179
TO GIVE ME SOME POINTERS.

167
00:07:21,179 --> 00:07:22,514
LOOSEN UP RIGHT HERE.

168
00:07:22,514 --> 00:07:24,716
SARAH--HER WALK
WAS, LIKE, TERRIBLE.

169
00:07:24,716 --> 00:07:25,984
IT NEEDED A LOT OF WORK.

170
00:07:25,984 --> 00:07:27,519
THAT WAS WAY TOO HARD.

171
00:07:27,519 --> 00:07:29,988
YOU HAVE SO MUCH MOTION
IN THE OCEAN.

172
00:07:29,988 --> 00:07:31,756
I FEEL LIKE I DON'T HAVE THAT,
YOU'RE ALL, LIKE...

173
00:07:31,756 --> 00:07:33,525
YOU HAVE TO RELAX.
YOUR KNEE IS LIKE THIS.

174
00:07:33,525 --> 00:07:35,527
CAN I SAY ONE THING
THAT I KINDA NOTICED?

175
00:07:35,527 --> 00:07:37,529
THEY ALWAYS WANT YOU TO TAKE
WIDER STRIDES AND BEING SHORT,

176
00:07:37,529 --> 00:07:39,531
WE HAVE TO TAKE--
IF YOU GIVE HER, LIKE,

177
00:07:39,531 --> 00:07:41,633
FIVE TIPS AND SAY "PUT IT
ALL TOGETHER," IT'S HARD.

178
00:07:41,633 --> 00:07:44,169
THIS IS STILL A COMPETITION,
SO I DIDN'T WANT TO, LIKE,

179
00:07:44,169 --> 00:07:46,538
GIVE HER EVERYTHING
TO MAKE THEM CHOOSE HER OVER ME.

180
00:07:46,538 --> 00:07:47,539
STEP WITH ME.

181
00:07:47,539 --> 00:07:50,074
BAM, BAM, BAM,

182
00:07:50,074 --> 00:07:51,109
BAM, BAM, BAM.

183
00:07:51,109 --> 00:07:52,377
OH, MY GOD, SARAH.

184
00:07:52,377 --> 00:07:54,879
YOU DON'T UNDERSTAND
HOW MUCH BETTER YOU ARE ALREADY.

185
00:07:54,879 --> 00:07:55,880
YOU FEEL BETTER?

186
00:07:55,880 --> 00:07:57,715
YEAH,
I FEEL REALLY CONFIDENT

187
00:07:57,715 --> 00:07:58,883
WHEN I'M NEXT TO YOU.

188
00:07:58,883 --> 00:08:00,451
IT'S RIDICULOUS HOW NICE
WE ARE TO EACH OTHER.

189
00:08:00,451 --> 00:08:01,452
WE'RE OUTTA CONTROL.

190
00:08:01,452 --> 00:08:02,453
IT'S LIKE--
WE'RE LIKE SISTERS.

191
00:08:02,453 --> 00:08:03,588
IT'S CRAZY.

192
00:08:03,588 --> 00:08:05,456
THIS IS NOT
AMERICA'S NEXT BEST FRIEND.

193
00:08:05,456 --> 00:08:07,759
IT'S "AMERICA'S
NEXT TOP MODEL."

194
00:08:07,759 --> 00:08:08,760
GO, POSER!

195
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:09,761
KEEP IT SIMPLE.

196
00:08:09,761 --> 00:08:10,762
OKAY.

197
00:08:10,762 --> 00:08:12,764
YOU GUYS ARE POSIN' OFF,
ALL RIGHT?

198
00:08:12,764 --> 00:08:14,832
LADIES, YOUR FIRST POSE
WE WANNA SEE IS ROCK STAR.

199
00:08:14,832 --> 00:08:17,168
THREE, TWO, ONE.

200
00:08:17,168 --> 00:08:20,838
OH! TATIANA!

201
00:08:20,838 --> 00:08:22,840
(All taking at once)

202
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:24,709
THE COMPETITION IS GETTING
MORE FIERCE.

203
00:08:24,709 --> 00:08:28,046
IT'S JUST, LIKE, BRINGING
MY CONFIDENCE DOWN A LITTLE BIT.

204
00:08:28,046 --> 00:08:30,782
I'M TRYING TO CONNECT WITH
THE OTHER GIRLS, BUT, I MEAN,

205
00:08:30,782 --> 00:08:31,916
IT'S HARD SOMETIMES.

206
00:08:31,916 --> 00:08:33,451
HEY, WE GOT TYRA MAIL!

207
00:08:33,451 --> 00:08:35,720
OH, YEAH.

208
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:37,655
OPEN IT AND READ IT.

209
00:08:37,655 --> 00:08:39,791
"WHICH AISLE WILL HAVE
TODAY'S SPECIAL?

210
00:08:39,791 --> 00:08:41,426
BE READY AT 6:45 A.M."

211
00:08:41,426 --> 00:08:42,427
OH!

212
00:08:42,427 --> 00:08:43,428
THAT'S EARLY.

213
00:08:43,428 --> 00:08:44,428
I'M GETTING UP AT 5:00.

214
00:08:44,428 --> 00:08:45,430
LET'S GO.

215
00:08:45,430 --> 00:08:47,465
THAT'S BEFORE 7.

216
00:08:47,465 --> 00:08:49,366
(alarm beeping)

217
00:08:52,403 --> 00:08:54,405
WE TRY TO FIGURE OUT
TYRA MAIL.

218
00:08:54,405 --> 00:08:56,808
AND WE NEVER GET IT RIGHT.

219
00:08:56,808 --> 00:08:59,344
OH, MY GOD.

220
00:08:59,344 --> 00:09:00,311
KMART.

221
00:09:00,311 --> 00:09:01,679
YES.

222
00:09:01,679 --> 00:09:03,982
THAT'S MY FAVORITE
SHOPPING SPOT.

223
00:09:03,982 --> 00:09:05,016
KMART?

224
00:09:05,016 --> 00:09:06,417
WHAT ARE WE GONNA DO
IN KMART?

225
00:09:06,417 --> 00:09:09,120
WHAT IS WE GETTIN' INTO?

226
00:09:09,120 --> 00:09:10,321
OH!

227
00:09:15,326 --> 00:09:16,694
WE'RE PULLING UP
TO OUR MYSTERY LOCATION

228
00:09:16,694 --> 00:09:19,931
FROM OUR TYRA MAIL,
AND WE SEE KMART.

229
00:09:19,931 --> 00:09:21,966
THE LAST PLACE I THOUGHT
WE'D BE BE GOING WAS K-MART,

230
00:09:21,966 --> 00:09:23,034
BUT, HEY,
I DON'T CARE, IT'S K-MART.

231
00:09:23,034 --> 00:09:24,102
I'VE BEEN THERE
A MILLION TIMES.

232
00:09:24,102 --> 00:09:25,870
♪♪♪

233
00:09:25,870 --> 00:09:27,538
ATTENTION ALL SHOPPERS,

234
00:09:27,538 --> 00:09:30,441
ATTENTION ALL SHOPPERS,
DUEL RUNWAY CHALLENGE

235
00:09:30,441 --> 00:09:33,144
IN AISLES ONE AND TWO.

236
00:09:33,144 --> 00:09:35,113
SO GOOD MORNING, GIRLS,
AND WELCOME.

237
00:09:35,113 --> 00:09:36,114
GOOD MORNING.

238
00:09:36,114 --> 00:09:38,116
A TOP MODEL CAN SELL
AN EVERYDAY ITEM

239
00:09:38,116 --> 00:09:39,884
AS SOMETHING FABULOUS.

240
00:09:39,884 --> 00:09:42,587
AND WHAT BETTER PLACE TO FIND
THINGS THAT YOU NEED EVERY DAY

241
00:09:42,587 --> 00:09:44,022
THAN HERE?

242
00:09:44,022 --> 00:09:47,525
WE LEARNED THE PREVIOUS DAY
HOW TO WALK WITH AN ACCESSORY.

243
00:09:47,525 --> 00:09:50,028
KMART PROVIDES
ANY KIND OF ACCESSORY,

244
00:09:50,028 --> 00:09:51,963
SO IT'S COMPLETELY FITTING.

245
00:09:51,963 --> 00:09:53,398
TODAY I BROUGHT
MY YOUNG FRIEND SANDI BASS...

246
00:09:53,398 --> 00:09:54,399
HELLO.

247
00:09:54,399 --> 00:09:56,401
WHO IS ONE
OF THE ORIGINAL MODELS

248
00:09:56,401 --> 00:09:58,136
FROM THE HOUSE OF GIVENCHY.

249
00:09:58,136 --> 00:10:00,138
SHE HAS WORKED
WITH EVERY MAJOR DESIGNER.

250
00:10:00,138 --> 00:10:02,140
YESTERDAY YOU HAD
A LITTLE RUNWAY CRASH COURSE.

251
00:10:02,140 --> 00:10:04,542
AND TODAY, WE'RE GONNA
PUT THAT TO THE TEST.

252
00:10:04,542 --> 00:10:05,643
THIS IS A CHALLENGE.

253
00:10:05,643 --> 00:10:08,546
A DUEL RUNWAY CHALLENGE.

254
00:10:08,546 --> 00:10:10,581
YOU'RE GOING TO BE DUELING
WITH EACH OTHER.

255
00:10:10,581 --> 00:10:12,784
ONE OF YOU WILL BE ELIMINATED.

256
00:10:12,784 --> 00:10:15,620
THERE CAN ONLY BE
ONE WINNER, OKAY?

257
00:10:15,620 --> 00:10:16,621
SHALL WE GET STARTED?

258
00:10:16,621 --> 00:10:17,655
YES.

259
00:10:17,655 --> 00:10:18,656
SANDI?

260
00:10:18,656 --> 00:10:19,857
HIT IT.

261
00:10:19,857 --> 00:10:21,826
♪♪♪

262
00:10:21,826 --> 00:10:24,362
YOU GUYS HAVE TO GO FASTER
THAN THIS, REALLY.

263
00:10:24,362 --> 00:10:27,699
CHRISTINA AND BRITTANY
TO THE FRONT, PLEASE.

264
00:10:27,699 --> 00:10:30,568
♪♪♪

265
00:10:30,568 --> 00:10:33,871
YESTERDAY J. SAID THAT
I'M TOO SEXY.

266
00:10:33,871 --> 00:10:35,673
HMM. LET ME SEE.

267
00:10:35,673 --> 00:10:37,175
BYE, BRITTANY.

268
00:10:37,175 --> 00:10:38,209
(buzzer)

269
00:10:38,209 --> 00:10:40,478
AGAIN, TOO SEXY.

270
00:10:40,478 --> 00:10:42,480
BRANDY'S WEARING
A FUCHSIA WRAP BLOUSE

271
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:43,981
AND A FRYING PAN.

272
00:10:43,981 --> 00:10:45,216
HOW FABULOUS.

273
00:10:45,216 --> 00:10:46,984
NAIMA IS WEARING
A FUCHSIA BLOUSE

274
00:10:46,984 --> 00:10:51,989
AND A SPONGE MOP, MOP,
MOP, MOP AND FRY, FRY, FRY.

275
00:10:51,989 --> 00:10:53,291
(buzzer)

276
00:10:53,291 --> 00:10:55,026
MISS BRANDY, JUST STEP OVER HERE
TO MY RIGHT, PLEASE.

277
00:10:55,026 --> 00:10:58,896
THANK YOU.

278
00:10:58,896 --> 00:11:00,898
SIMPLE, SIMPLE, SIMPLE.

279
00:11:00,898 --> 00:11:02,667
CHIC, CHIC, CHIC.

280
00:11:02,667 --> 00:11:04,202
NOELLE, BYE.

281
00:11:04,202 --> 00:11:06,838
(buzzer)

282
00:11:06,838 --> 00:11:08,506
CAN I PLEASE
HAVE MICHELLE

283
00:11:08,506 --> 00:11:10,575
OVER IN THE LAYAWAY
DEPARTMENT.

284
00:11:10,575 --> 00:11:13,111
(buzzer)

285
00:11:13,111 --> 00:11:14,278
- HOW YOU DOING?
- GOOD.

286
00:11:14,278 --> 00:11:15,680
OKAY, GOOD.

287
00:11:15,680 --> 00:11:19,584
KAHLEN'S WEARING A FUCHSIA
LONG SLEEVE BLOUSE AND A MOP.

288
00:11:19,584 --> 00:11:22,453
IS THE MOP ON HER HEAD
OR IN HER HANDS?

289
00:11:22,453 --> 00:11:24,288
LLUVY IS WEARING
BLACK CROPPED TEE

290
00:11:24,288 --> 00:11:27,325
AND BLACK PLATFORMS
AND A BATH AND BOWL SCRUBBER.

291
00:11:27,325 --> 00:11:28,626
LLUVY.

292
00:11:28,626 --> 00:11:29,894
(buzzer)

293
00:11:29,894 --> 00:11:33,898
TATIANA AND KEENYAH
TO SECURITY, PLEASE, THANK YOU.

294
00:11:33,898 --> 00:11:35,366
TATIANA, TA-TA.

295
00:11:35,366 --> 00:11:37,368
(buzzer)

296
00:11:37,368 --> 00:11:40,838
SARAH WAS IN A WHOLE CATEGORY
BY HERSELF BECAUSE SHE'S SLOW.

297
00:11:40,838 --> 00:11:42,540
SARAH, I NEED
SOME MORE SPUNK.

298
00:11:42,540 --> 00:11:44,675
WALK AS THOUGH
YOU'RE WALKING THROUGH HELL

299
00:11:44,675 --> 00:11:46,577
IN GASOLINE-SOAKED PAJAMAS.

300
00:11:46,577 --> 00:11:49,213
UNFORTUNATELY,
WE DO NOT DO RETURNS

301
00:11:49,213 --> 00:11:50,214
WITHOUT RECEIPTS.

302
00:11:50,214 --> 00:11:51,449
THANK YOU.

303
00:11:51,449 --> 00:11:52,450
(buzzer)

304
00:11:52,450 --> 00:11:53,584
I JUST KIND OF FELT LIKE,

305
00:11:53,584 --> 00:11:54,619
"OKAY, DAY TWO WITH MISS J.,
AND I'VE LEARNED

306
00:11:54,619 --> 00:11:55,620
ABSOLUTELY NOTHING."

307
00:11:55,620 --> 00:11:56,821
SO IT'S A LITTLE
NERVE-RACKING.

308
00:11:56,821 --> 00:11:58,423
THIS IS GREAT
FOR THAT LEATHER SKIRT.

309
00:11:58,423 --> 00:12:00,158
I LOVE IT.

310
00:12:00,158 --> 00:12:02,293
CLADUMP. CLADUMP. CLADUMP.

311
00:12:02,293 --> 00:12:03,528
KAHLEN.

312
00:12:03,528 --> 00:12:04,529
(buzzer)

313
00:12:04,529 --> 00:12:05,897
ATTENTION, TIFFANY,

314
00:12:05,897 --> 00:12:08,433
THE SHOULDER BAG
SHOULD NOT BE HELD

315
00:12:08,433 --> 00:12:10,401
AWAY FROM YOU AS THOUGH
YOU'RE CARRYING A DIRTY PAIR

316
00:12:10,401 --> 00:12:11,602
OF UNDERWEAR.

317
00:12:11,602 --> 00:12:12,937
THANK YOU.

318
00:12:12,937 --> 00:12:14,806
(buzzer)

319
00:12:14,806 --> 00:12:17,175
CAN WE PLEASE HAVE CHRISTINA
OVER IN LAYAWAY?

320
00:12:17,175 --> 00:12:19,277
(buzzer)

321
00:12:19,277 --> 00:12:21,312
KEENYAH, GO FIND
YOUR BABY'S DADDY.

322
00:12:21,312 --> 00:12:22,313
(buzzer)

323
00:12:22,313 --> 00:12:24,816
THE DUEL CHALLENGE FINAL

324
00:12:24,816 --> 00:12:27,018
IS NOW TAKING PLACE
IN AISLES ONE AND TWO.

325
00:12:27,018 --> 00:12:29,053
HIT IT.

326
00:12:29,053 --> 00:12:32,924
I'M WALKING WITH REBECCA,
AND ALL I'M THINKING IS,

327
00:12:32,924 --> 00:12:36,794
"THERE'S THIS BITCH NEXT TO ME,
AND IT'S EITHER HER OR IT'S ME,

328
00:12:36,794 --> 00:12:38,095
AND IT'S GOT TO BE ME."

329
00:12:38,095 --> 00:12:39,230
I AM REALLY FEELING
THE PRESSURE.

330
00:12:39,230 --> 00:12:40,865
EVERYTHING I DO
IS A COMPETITION.

331
00:12:40,865 --> 00:12:42,366
I ALWAYS WANT TO BE
THE BEST.

332
00:12:42,366 --> 00:12:44,936
I HATE TO LOSE.

333
00:12:44,936 --> 00:12:48,940
AND THE WINNER IS...

334
00:12:48,940 --> 00:12:53,211
MISS BECKY.

335
00:12:53,211 --> 00:12:54,679
CONGRATULATIONS.

336
00:12:54,679 --> 00:12:55,947
TO KNOW THAT
THE BEST RUNWAY COACH

337
00:12:55,947 --> 00:12:57,648
IN THE WORLD THINKS
THAT I'VE GOT A GOOD WALK...

338
00:12:57,648 --> 00:12:58,950
I WAS THE WINNER.

339
00:12:58,950 --> 00:13:01,385
EVERYBODY KNOWS WHERE WE STAND,
AND I WAS AT THE TOP.

340
00:13:01,385 --> 00:13:04,689
SO FOR TODAY'S WIN, YOU GET
TO MEET A FAMOUS SHOE DESIGNER,

341
00:13:04,689 --> 00:13:08,960
AND YOU GET TO CHOOSE
FIVE FRIENDS TO GO WITH YOU.

342
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:10,394
FIVE FRIENDS?

343
00:13:10,394 --> 00:13:13,331
MISS KAHLEN, MISS SARAH,

344
00:13:13,331 --> 00:13:16,934
MISS NOELLE, MISS LLUVY.

345
00:13:16,934 --> 00:13:18,636
LAST ONE,
WHO IS IT GOING TO BE?

346
00:13:18,636 --> 00:13:20,738
I'M GONNA PICK NAIMA
BECAUSE SHE WAS DAMN CLOSE.

347
00:13:20,738 --> 00:13:21,739
SHE WAS A HARD COMPETITOR.

348
00:13:21,739 --> 00:13:23,207
FOR THE GIRLS
WHO DIDN'T MAKE

349
00:13:23,207 --> 00:13:27,445
THIS WONDERFUL LINE OVER HERE,
YOU GET TO SERVICE THE GIRLS.

350
00:13:27,445 --> 00:13:29,113
- SERVICE?
- SERVICE.

351
00:13:29,113 --> 00:13:31,482
THAT'S AN INTERESTING WORD.

352
00:13:31,482 --> 00:13:33,484
SERVE THEM?
WHAT IS THIS?

353
00:13:33,484 --> 00:13:35,086
I THOUGHT
I DID PRETTY GOOD.

354
00:13:35,086 --> 00:13:36,587
WHY SHOULD I HAVE TO
SERVE ANYBODY?

355
00:13:36,587 --> 00:13:37,955
I THINK
THEY SHOULD BE SERVING ME.

356
00:13:37,955 --> 00:13:39,023
OKAY, GIRLS, THANK YOU.

357
00:13:39,023 --> 00:13:40,458
(applause)

358
00:13:40,458 --> 00:13:41,592
GREAT JOB.

359
00:13:41,592 --> 00:13:46,297
♪♪♪

360
00:13:46,297 --> 00:13:49,300
I'M REALLY, REALLY EXCITED
ABOUT MEETING THE SHOE DESIGNER.

361
00:13:49,300 --> 00:13:50,835
WE DON'T KNOW
WHO IT IS YET.

362
00:13:50,835 --> 00:13:52,904
OH, MY GOSH!

363
00:13:52,904 --> 00:13:54,238
THOSE ARE SICK.

364
00:13:54,238 --> 00:13:57,875
♪♪♪

365
00:13:57,875 --> 00:14:00,144
STUART WEITZMAN'S SHOES
ARE GORGEOUS.

366
00:14:00,144 --> 00:14:01,546
OH, MY GOSH.

367
00:14:01,546 --> 00:14:03,681
TO JUST LOOK AROUND HIS STORE
JUST GETS MY HEART

368
00:14:03,681 --> 00:14:05,049
BEATING A LITTLE FASTER.

369
00:14:05,049 --> 00:14:06,884
WELCOME TO SHOE HEAVEN.

370
00:14:06,884 --> 00:14:08,886
I AM STUART WEITZMAN.

371
00:14:08,886 --> 00:14:10,621
AND, REBECCA,
YOU GET TO PICK OUT

372
00:14:10,621 --> 00:14:14,625
A BEAUTIFUL PAIR OF SHOES
AND FIVE OF YOUR FRIENDS

373
00:14:14,625 --> 00:14:18,829
ALSO GET TO PICK OUT
A BEAUTIFUL PAIR OF SHOES...

374
00:14:18,829 --> 00:14:20,932
WHILE THE REST OF YOU LADIES,
YOU'RE GONNA SERVE THEM

375
00:14:20,932 --> 00:14:23,167
AND TREAT THEM LIKE THE QUEENS
THAT THEY WILL BE

376
00:14:23,167 --> 00:14:24,268
WHEN THEY WEAR THESE SHOES.

377
00:14:24,268 --> 00:14:25,403
THAT'S NOT FAIR.

378
00:14:25,403 --> 00:14:26,404
SOME OF THOSE GIRLS
DIDN'T DO ANYTHING.

379
00:14:26,404 --> 00:14:27,772
THEY DID NOT EVEN WALK
THAT GOOD.

380
00:14:27,772 --> 00:14:29,807
AND HERE THEY ARE GETTING
A BRAND-NEW PAIR OF SHOES,

381
00:14:29,807 --> 00:14:31,943
AWESOME LIKE...

382
00:14:31,943 --> 00:14:33,511
IT WAS JUST WRONG.

383
00:14:33,511 --> 00:14:36,213
JAY, WHY DON'T YOU TAKE
THE UNLUCKY LADIES

384
00:14:36,213 --> 00:14:37,949
AND SHOW WHERE
THE STOCK ROOM IS.

385
00:14:37,949 --> 00:14:40,251
AND IT'S A GOOD THING
SOME OF YOU ARE IN JEANS.

386
00:14:40,251 --> 00:14:42,320
YOU ALWAYS HAVE TO BE VERY,
VERY CAREFUL

387
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:43,554
THAT THERE'S NO ONE IN HERE.

388
00:14:43,554 --> 00:14:45,590
- OKAY.
- AND THEN YOU JUST PULL IT.

389
00:14:45,590 --> 00:14:48,259
I DIDN'T LIKE THE THING
THEY KEPT THE SHOES IN.

390
00:14:48,259 --> 00:14:51,395
MY ONE WORST FEAR
IS BEING, LIKE, SQUISHED.

391
00:14:51,395 --> 00:14:53,965
THE SHOES
ARE ACCORDING TO COLORS

392
00:14:53,965 --> 00:14:55,266
AND THEY'RE ALPHABETIZED.

393
00:14:55,266 --> 00:14:57,969
THAT'S WHY YOU MUST KNOW
THE NAME OF THE SHOE.

394
00:14:57,969 --> 00:14:59,337
I HOPE
I DON'T COME DOWNSTAIRS

395
00:14:59,337 --> 00:15:01,038
AND EVERY GIRL HAS, LIKE,
30 PAIRS OF SHOES AND ARE LIKE,

396
00:15:01,038 --> 00:15:02,773
"GO GET A 9 1/2
IN EACH OF THESE."

397
00:15:02,773 --> 00:15:04,842
♪♪♪

398
00:15:04,842 --> 00:15:08,746
IN OKLAHOMA, WE DO HAVE SHOES,
BUT NOTHING LIKE THIS.

399
00:15:08,746 --> 00:15:10,748
STUART WEITZMAN--
WE WERE GONNA GET TO TAKE

400
00:15:10,748 --> 00:15:12,249
A PAIR OF THOSE SHOES HOME.

401
00:15:12,249 --> 00:15:14,919
OH, MY GOD.
ALL OF US, TEARS IN OUR EYES.

402
00:15:14,919 --> 00:15:16,120
IT WAS ABSOLUTELY AMAZING.

403
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:17,321
THIS IS THE BEST DAY
OF MY LIFE.

404
00:15:17,321 --> 00:15:19,457
THIS IS AMAZING.
THIS IS LIKE A CINDERELLA STORY.

405
00:15:19,457 --> 00:15:21,392
I AM GLAD I'M NOT
ONE OF THOSE GIRLS

406
00:15:21,392 --> 00:15:23,060
THAT ARE HAVING TO SERVE US.

407
00:15:23,060 --> 00:15:24,662
DID SOMETHING BAD HAPPEN?

408
00:15:24,662 --> 00:15:27,231
NO, I WAS IN THERE
AND SOMEONE WAS CLOSING IT

409
00:15:27,231 --> 00:15:29,333
AND IT SCARED THE... OF ME.

410
00:15:29,333 --> 00:15:30,501
MICHELLE, YOU DON'T NEED
TO BE OVER HERE, SERIOUSLY.

411
00:15:30,501 --> 00:15:31,836
NO, NO, NO, NO, NO.

412
00:15:31,836 --> 00:15:33,104
NO, SERIOUSLY, YOU'VE ALREADY
HAD A BAD EXPERIENCE.

413
00:15:33,104 --> 00:15:34,839
I DON'T CARE,
IF YOU GUYS JUST--

414
00:15:34,839 --> 00:15:38,776
I CAN DO IT IF THEY DON'T
DO THAT AGAIN AT ALL.

415
00:15:38,776 --> 00:15:41,278
MICHELLE--SHE WALKS
INSIDE HER SHOE SHELVES,

416
00:15:41,278 --> 00:15:42,446
AND SHE'S LIKE,
"I'M GOING INSIDE HERE

417
00:15:42,446 --> 00:15:43,648
SO NOBODY CLOSE IT."

418
00:15:43,648 --> 00:15:45,282
AND I LEAN IN
LIKE I'M GOING TO CLOSE IT,

419
00:15:45,282 --> 00:15:47,518
BARELY, AND, LIKE,
TOUCH THE KNOB,

420
00:15:47,518 --> 00:15:49,887
AND I GUESS SHE JUST HEARD
THE SHELF MOVE,

421
00:15:49,887 --> 00:15:51,422
AND SHE WENT CRAZY.

422
00:15:51,422 --> 00:15:53,691
I TOLD YOU I WAS IN HERE,
AND I KNOW YOU WERE PLAYING,

423
00:15:53,691 --> 00:15:55,359
BUT YOU STILL DID IT.

424
00:15:55,359 --> 00:15:58,095
I JUST DON'T--DON'T DO IT AGAIN
AND I'LL BE FINE.

425
00:15:58,095 --> 00:16:02,767
IT'S JUST...

426
00:16:02,767 --> 00:16:05,236
MICHELLE, SHE'S USUALLY
VERY QUIET AND SOFT.

427
00:16:05,236 --> 00:16:06,470
AND WE WERE LIKE,
"WHAT THE HELL IS THIS?

428
00:16:06,470 --> 00:16:08,606
- WHERE'S MICHELLE?"
- YOU WAS JUST PLAYING.

429
00:16:08,606 --> 00:16:10,574
I REALLY, SERIOUSLY WAS.

430
00:16:10,574 --> 00:16:12,043
IT WAS JUST LIKE THIS.

431
00:16:12,043 --> 00:16:13,344
- IT DIDN'T EVEN MOVE.
- IT WAS JUST LIKE THIS.

432
00:16:13,344 --> 00:16:15,079
I HAVE NO IDEA
WHY SHE FLIPPED LIKE THAT.

433
00:16:15,079 --> 00:16:16,781
THAT WAS CRAZY.

434
00:16:16,781 --> 00:16:18,883
LITERALLY, IT WAS NUTS.

435
00:16:18,883 --> 00:16:21,152
I KIND OF FEEL
THAT WALL BUILDING

436
00:16:21,152 --> 00:16:22,520
BETWEEN MYSELF
AND THE OTHER GIRLS.

437
00:16:22,520 --> 00:16:24,855
WHEN I'M AT A LOW POINT,
YOU KNOW, FREAKING OUT

438
00:16:24,855 --> 00:16:27,825
OR STRESSED OUT,
I HATE SHOWING THAT TO PEOPLE.

439
00:16:27,825 --> 00:16:29,427
I HATE WHEN PEOPLE SEE THAT.

440
00:16:29,427 --> 00:16:31,395
TIME TO GET THE SHOES,
HALLELUJAH.

441
00:16:31,395 --> 00:16:32,496
TIME TO GET TO WORK.

442
00:16:32,496 --> 00:16:34,231
READY?
HERE WE GO.

443
00:16:34,231 --> 00:16:35,399
BYE, SISTER.

444
00:16:35,399 --> 00:16:38,135
I THINK I'M GOING, TOO.

445
00:16:38,135 --> 00:16:39,570
HI, MY NAME IS MICHELLE.

446
00:16:39,570 --> 00:16:40,838
HOW MAY I BE OF SERVICE?

447
00:16:40,838 --> 00:16:42,573
MICHELLE--
SO HAPPY ONE MINUTE,

448
00:16:42,573 --> 00:16:44,475
THEN IT'S JUST LIKE
MICHELLE SNAPS,

449
00:16:44,475 --> 00:16:47,211
AND HER MIND JUST CUTS OFF
AND THEN SHE'S BACK TO,

450
00:16:47,211 --> 00:16:48,179
"OH, I'M BUBBLY."

451
00:16:48,179 --> 00:16:49,413
MICHELLE IS CRAZY.

452
00:16:49,413 --> 00:16:51,082
I WOULD LIKE PEGGY SUE.

453
00:16:51,082 --> 00:16:52,349
THE METEORIC.

454
00:16:52,349 --> 00:16:54,285
WHAT KIND OF SHOES WILL YOU
BE TRYING ON TODAY?

455
00:16:54,285 --> 00:16:56,787
THIS IS MARRY ME, SIZE 9.

456
00:16:56,787 --> 00:16:58,823
RAMBLING ROSE.
OH, IN GOLD.

457
00:16:58,823 --> 00:17:00,925
AND METEORIC IN GOLD.

458
00:17:00,925 --> 00:17:02,760
NEXT SHOE.
RIBBON AIR.

459
00:17:02,760 --> 00:17:05,129
BECCA'S ATTITUDE
WAS VERY SNOOTY.

460
00:17:05,129 --> 00:17:07,198
ALL OF US FELT IT,
NONE OF US LIKED IT.

461
00:17:07,198 --> 00:17:08,332
ARE YOU SATISFIED?

462
00:17:08,332 --> 00:17:09,333
I'M WONDERFUL,
THANK YOU.

463
00:17:09,333 --> 00:17:10,501
- ARE YOU SURE?
- MM-HMM.

464
00:17:10,501 --> 00:17:12,670
ARE YOU SURE THAT YOU'RE
SURE THAT YOU'RE SURE?

465
00:17:12,670 --> 00:17:14,505
I'M TRYING TO BE
A GRACIOUS WINNER.

466
00:17:14,505 --> 00:17:16,373
I CAN'T WORRY ABOUT
EVERYONE ELSE'S FEELINGS.

467
00:17:16,373 --> 00:17:19,143
I WORKED MY BUTT OFF
ON THE RUNWAY, AND I'M GONNA

468
00:17:19,143 --> 00:17:20,411
ENJOY EVERY SINGLE MINUTE
OF THIS.

469
00:17:20,411 --> 00:17:23,414
OH, NO, I DROPPED
A STRAWBERRY LEAF IN MY WATER.

470
00:17:23,414 --> 00:17:25,950
CAN I HAVE SOME MORE?

471
00:17:25,950 --> 00:17:31,222
HONESTLY, FROM THE HEART,
THEY MADE US FEEL LIKE CRAP.

472
00:17:31,222 --> 00:17:34,191
IT'S MY BIGGEST CHALLENGE
TO WORK ON MY ATTITUDE

473
00:17:34,191 --> 00:17:37,661
AND NOT SAY ANYTHING TO ANYBODY,
BUT I'M IRRITATED.

474
00:17:37,661 --> 00:17:39,063
Y'ALL DONE MADE ME MAD.

475
00:17:39,063 --> 00:17:40,464
MISS REBECCA.

476
00:17:40,464 --> 00:17:43,134
- HELLO, YOU GOT MY SHOES?
- YES, I DO.

477
00:17:43,134 --> 00:17:44,668
THESE ARE MADE
SO THAT YOU CAN TIE THEM

478
00:17:44,668 --> 00:17:50,508
TWO WAYS, AND I WOULD SAY 8 1/2
MIGHT BE BETTER FOR YOU.

479
00:17:50,508 --> 00:17:52,143
I THINK EVERY GIRL
IS A LITTLE JEALOUS

480
00:17:52,143 --> 00:17:53,244
THAT THEY DIDN'T GET
A PAIR OF SHOES.

481
00:17:53,244 --> 00:17:54,411
THERE'S NOTHING I CAN DO
ABOUT IT.

482
00:17:54,411 --> 00:17:56,247
I CAN'T CHOOSE EVERYBODY.

483
00:17:56,247 --> 00:17:59,683
YOU ARE A GENIUS.

484
00:17:59,683 --> 00:18:02,253
MISS REBECCA.

485
00:18:02,253 --> 00:18:04,054
SO HOW ABOUT,
LIKE, A BIG HUG?

486
00:18:04,054 --> 00:18:06,023
OH!

487
00:18:06,023 --> 00:18:07,825
STUART HUGGED ALL OF THEM
AND WAS, LIKE,

488
00:18:07,825 --> 00:18:10,427
"OH, GOOD LUCK, GIRLS,
CONGRATULATIONS."

489
00:18:10,427 --> 00:18:13,697
WE'RE JUST
THESE HUGE LOSERS WHO STUNK.

490
00:18:13,697 --> 00:18:17,768
IT JUST WASN'T
A FRIENDLY FEELING.

491
00:18:17,768 --> 00:18:20,137
I CAN FEEL
A LITTLE BIT MORE TENSION.

492
00:18:20,137 --> 00:18:22,439
I THINK THERE REALLY IS A LINE
THAT'S STARTING TO BE DRAWN.

493
00:18:22,439 --> 00:18:24,642
THIS IS COMPETITION
AND I'M SORRY,

494
00:18:24,642 --> 00:18:26,343
BUT I'M NOT HERE TO FEED
YOUR EGO,

495
00:18:26,343 --> 00:18:28,412
I'M HERE FOR ME.

496
00:18:28,412 --> 00:18:30,848
BRANDY, I'MA NEED YOU
TO KNOW, WE'VE GOT TYRA MAIL.

497
00:18:30,848 --> 00:18:33,484
MICHELLE'S
IN THE OTHER ROOM.

498
00:18:33,484 --> 00:18:36,554
MICHELLE JUST REALLY STAYS AWAY
FROM EVERYBODY A LOT.

499
00:18:36,554 --> 00:18:39,423
"CAN YOU WORK
WITH TEN OTHER BITCHES?

500
00:18:39,423 --> 00:18:41,025
BE READY AT 7:15."

501
00:18:41,025 --> 00:18:45,029
SHUT UP, TEN GIRLS
FROM THE LAST SEASONS?

502
00:18:45,029 --> 00:18:46,964
OH, YEAH.

503
00:18:46,964 --> 00:18:48,833
MICHELLE IS GETTING
VERY WEIRD.

504
00:18:48,833 --> 00:18:52,136
SHE SEEMS TO BLOW UP
ON PEOPLE RANDOMLY.

505
00:18:52,136 --> 00:18:55,439
I WENT TO MICHELLE'S ROOM
TO CONFRONT HER

506
00:18:55,439 --> 00:18:56,907
ABOUT HER ATTITUDE.

507
00:19:04,148 --> 00:19:08,052
ME AND TIFFANY, WE HEAR
MICHELLE SAYING SOMETHING,

508
00:19:08,052 --> 00:19:11,088
AND THEN
WE START EAVESDROPPING,

509
00:19:11,088 --> 00:19:13,991
TRYING TO SEE EXACTLY
WHAT SHE'S TALKING ABOUT.

510
00:19:13,991 --> 00:19:17,428
YEAH, BECAUSE I'VE BEEN,
LIKE, HIDING IT FOR SO LONG.

511
00:19:17,428 --> 00:19:19,096
I MEAN,
IT'S EATING ME UP INSIDE

512
00:19:19,096 --> 00:19:20,497
BECAUSE I CAN'T GET IT OUT.

513
00:19:20,497 --> 00:19:23,100
I THINK THE REASON
I WAS RELUCTANT TO,

514
00:19:23,100 --> 00:19:26,103
LIKE, TELL EVERYONE IS
BECAUSE HOW PEOPLE WOULD REACT.

515
00:19:26,103 --> 00:19:28,706
I CAN GUARANTEE YOU THAT
EVERY SINGLE GIRL IN THIS HOUSE

516
00:19:28,706 --> 00:19:31,642
IS NOT GOING TO LOOK AT YOU
A STITCH DIFFERENTLY

517
00:19:31,642 --> 00:19:34,245
BECAUSE YOU'RE BI.

518
00:19:34,245 --> 00:19:36,347
I HEARD HER SAY, "I'M GAY,"
YOU KNOW,

519
00:19:36,347 --> 00:19:38,849
SO I WAS LIKE, "WHAT?"

520
00:19:45,656 --> 00:19:48,092
♪♪♪

521
00:19:48,092 --> 00:19:49,326
I THINK THE REASON

522
00:19:49,326 --> 00:19:51,328
I WAS RELUCTANT TO, LIKE,
TELL EVERYONE IS BECAUSE

523
00:19:51,328 --> 00:19:53,931
HOW PEOPLE WOULD REACT.

524
00:19:53,931 --> 00:19:55,933
MICHELLE AND NOELLE
WERE IN THE ROOM TALKING,

525
00:19:55,933 --> 00:19:57,935
AND I WAS EAVESDROPPING TILL
I HEARD HER SAY, "I'M GAY."

526
00:19:57,935 --> 00:20:00,971
YOU KNOW,
SO I WAS LIKE, "WHAT?"

527
00:20:00,971 --> 00:20:02,640
NO, I DON'T KNOW. YOU GAY?

528
00:20:02,640 --> 00:20:03,641
SHE'S BI.

529
00:20:03,641 --> 00:20:05,643
THERE'S NOTHING WRONG
WITH THAT.

530
00:20:05,643 --> 00:20:06,977
SHE FEELS LIKE SHE'S HAD TO
HIDE THIS FOR SO LONG.

531
00:20:06,977 --> 00:20:08,112
THIS IS NOT ACCEPTED.

532
00:20:09,947 --> 00:20:11,582
YOU THINK ABOUT ME?

533
00:20:11,582 --> 00:20:13,984
I DON'T HAVE A PROBLEM
WITH BISEXUALITY.

534
00:20:13,984 --> 00:20:15,986
I THINK MICHELLE JUST NEEDS
TO KNOW WE'RE GONNA ACCEPT HER

535
00:20:15,986 --> 00:20:17,922
EITHER WAY.

536
00:20:17,922 --> 00:20:19,757
SO HOW DO YOU KNOW
YOU LIKE A GIRL?

537
00:20:19,757 --> 00:20:20,925
HOW DO YOU KNOW?

538
00:20:20,925 --> 00:20:23,294
MY FIRST RELATIONSHIP
WITH ANOTHER WOMAN,

539
00:20:23,294 --> 00:20:26,530
AND THE FIRST TIME WE KISSED,
WE SAT THERE AND WE'RE LIKE...

540
00:20:26,530 --> 00:20:27,631
EW. OH NO.

541
00:20:27,631 --> 00:20:31,068
UM, NO.

542
00:20:31,068 --> 00:20:33,070
AND, I MEAN, SHE'S LIKE,
"YOU KNOW,

543
00:20:33,070 --> 00:20:34,238
THAT WASN'T THAT BAD,"
AND I WAS LIKE,

544
00:20:34,238 --> 00:20:35,506
"NO, ACTUALLY IT WASN'T."

545
00:20:35,506 --> 00:20:37,241
MICHELLE'S OUTBURSTS
MAKE A LOT MORE SENSE TO ME

546
00:20:37,241 --> 00:20:40,077
BECAUSE WHEN YOU'RE TRYING
TO HIDE A PART OF WHO YOU ARE,

547
00:20:40,077 --> 00:20:41,979
YOU'RE BOUND
TO HAVE FREAK-OUTS.

548
00:20:41,979 --> 00:20:46,684
MICHELLE, THE BEST THING
FOR YOU TO DO IS TELL IT.

549
00:20:46,684 --> 00:20:49,586
I'M REALLY GLAD THAT THEY
ALL JUST CAME TOGETHER FOR ME

550
00:20:49,586 --> 00:20:50,988
AND ACCEPTED ME.

551
00:20:50,988 --> 00:20:54,558
I JUST FEEL MORE CONFIDENT
AND I FEEL LIKE I CAN JUST BE

552
00:20:54,558 --> 00:20:55,993
MYSELF NOW.

553
00:20:55,993 --> 00:20:56,994
YOU'RE OKAY?

554
00:20:56,994 --> 00:20:57,995
YEAH, I'M GOOD. I'M GOOD.

555
00:20:57,995 --> 00:20:59,063
I'M A LOT BETTER NOW.

556
00:20:59,063 --> 00:21:00,664
YOU'RE GAY. OH.

557
00:21:00,664 --> 00:21:02,232
YEAH. YEP!

558
00:21:05,235 --> 00:21:08,572
♪♪♪

559
00:21:08,572 --> 00:21:09,640
TYRA MAIL SAID SOMETHING

560
00:21:09,640 --> 00:21:11,575
ABOUT WORKING WITH
TEN OTHER BITCHES.

561
00:21:11,575 --> 00:21:13,577
I'M LIKE, "I ALREADY GOT
TO WORK WITH THESE BITCHES."

562
00:21:13,577 --> 00:21:14,611
I DON'T NEED NO MORE.

563
00:21:15,612 --> 00:21:18,816
♪♪♪

564
00:21:18,816 --> 00:21:22,953
ON TODAY'S SHOOT DOING HAIR--
FABULOUS, FAMOUS DANILO.

565
00:21:22,953 --> 00:21:25,356
WITH MAKEUP,
WE HAVE MR. MATTHEW,

566
00:21:25,356 --> 00:21:26,690
WHO CAN PAINT ANYTHING.

567
00:21:26,690 --> 00:21:29,426
WARDROBE STYLIST
FOR ALL YOUR SHOOTS--Q.

568
00:21:29,426 --> 00:21:31,362
SHE'S GOT YOU ALL DOWN.

569
00:21:31,362 --> 00:21:33,530
AND LAST BUT NOT LEAST,
YOUR PHOTOGRAPHER

570
00:21:33,530 --> 00:21:34,631
FOR TODAY IS DANIELLE.

571
00:21:34,631 --> 00:21:36,133
HI!

572
00:21:36,133 --> 00:21:38,335
THIS SHOOT
IS FOR 1-800-FLOWERS.

573
00:21:38,335 --> 00:21:40,337
WE'RE GONNA START YOU GUYS
INTO HAIR AND MAKEUP,

574
00:21:40,337 --> 00:21:41,972
AND THEN YOUR CO-STARS
ARE SHOWING UP.

575
00:21:41,972 --> 00:21:42,973
LET'S GET TO WORK.

576
00:21:42,973 --> 00:21:44,408
♪♪♪

577
00:21:44,408 --> 00:21:45,709
I LOVE IT LONG.

578
00:21:45,709 --> 00:21:47,544
I'M JUST STILL TRYING
TO GET USED TO HOW TO DO IT.

579
00:21:47,544 --> 00:21:48,912
I'M REALLY FEELING
THE PRESSURE OF THE SHOOT.

580
00:21:48,912 --> 00:21:49,913
THIS IS WHAT IT'S
ALL ABOUT.

581
00:21:49,913 --> 00:21:51,081
THIS IS WHAT
WE'RE GETTING JUDGED ON.

582
00:21:51,081 --> 00:21:52,750
MAKE TYRA PROUD.

583
00:21:52,750 --> 00:21:55,652
(horn honking)

584
00:21:55,652 --> 00:21:57,488
(squealing and screaming)

585
00:21:57,488 --> 00:22:00,190
I'M HERE. HI, GIRLS.

586
00:22:00,190 --> 00:22:01,625
HI.

587
00:22:01,625 --> 00:22:03,761
WELCOME TO THE LOVELY
GRIFFITH PARK.

588
00:22:03,761 --> 00:22:05,496
THIS IS THE PARK THAT I USED
TO GO, OKAY,

589
00:22:05,496 --> 00:22:08,432
WITH MY LITTLE BOYFRIEND.

590
00:22:08,432 --> 00:22:12,503
WHO CAN GUESS NOW
WHAT THE TYRA MAIL... MEANS?

591
00:22:12,503 --> 00:22:15,506
YOU GUYS HAVE TO BE POSING
WITH TEN DOGGIES TODAY!

592
00:22:15,506 --> 00:22:16,874
(cheering)

593
00:22:16,874 --> 00:22:19,410
YOU GUYS WILL BE
WALKING THESE DOGS,

594
00:22:19,410 --> 00:22:22,413
CARRYING FLOWERS
AND LOOKING FIERCE!

595
00:22:22,413 --> 00:22:25,816
WHILE WE HAVE THIS GORGEOUS
MALE MODEL IN THE BACKGROUND.

596
00:22:25,816 --> 00:22:27,051
(screaming)

597
00:22:27,051 --> 00:22:28,685
WE'RE GONNA
HAVE FUN TODAY.

598
00:22:28,685 --> 00:22:29,686
YEAH.

599
00:22:29,686 --> 00:22:30,687
BYE, GUYS.

600
00:22:30,687 --> 00:22:32,456
BYE!

601
00:22:32,456 --> 00:22:34,291
I NEED FIERCE,
YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN?

602
00:22:34,291 --> 00:22:37,027
WORK IT. NOTHING HOOCHIE,
NOT LIKE YOU AT A SHOW PALACE.

603
00:22:37,027 --> 00:22:38,962
- OH, NOT LIKE THAT.
- YEAH, NOT LIKE THAT.

604
00:22:38,962 --> 00:22:41,999
IF THE DOG BITE ME,
I'M BITING THEM BACK.

605
00:22:41,999 --> 00:22:43,000
YEAH, RIGHT THERE.

606
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:44,268
YOU CAN GRAB THE FLOWERS.

607
00:22:44,268 --> 00:22:46,036
LIKE, YOU COULD BE LIKE THIS,
LIKE, "OOH, OKAY,

608
00:22:46,036 --> 00:22:47,604
PAPA'S BACK THERE,
HE'S CHECKING ME OUT."

609
00:22:49,940 --> 00:22:50,941
THAT'S THE POINT.

610
00:22:50,941 --> 00:22:53,277
UH-HUH,
BUT WITHOUT THE GHETTO FACE.

611
00:22:53,277 --> 00:22:54,511
- GOOD!
- THERE YOU GO.

612
00:22:54,511 --> 00:22:56,280
NOW YOU'RE GIVING ME
TOP MODEL.

613
00:22:56,280 --> 00:22:57,281
- WAS IT EASY?
- YOU LOOK REALLY PRETTY.

614
00:22:57,281 --> 00:22:58,649
HELL NO, IT WASN'T EASY!

615
00:22:58,649 --> 00:22:59,650
THAT'S WHAT
I WANTED TO KNOW.

616
00:22:59,650 --> 00:23:00,751
YOU'RE STANDING
WITH THE DOGS,

617
00:23:00,751 --> 00:23:02,653
BUT TRUST ME,
THEY CAN MOVE YOU.

618
00:23:02,653 --> 00:23:04,955
CHRISTINA,
I STILL NEED SOME RANGE.

619
00:23:04,955 --> 00:23:05,956
STRAIGHTEN THE FACE OUT!

620
00:23:05,956 --> 00:23:07,324
WORK YOUR FACE.

621
00:23:07,324 --> 00:23:10,227
CHRISTINA, WHEN SHE EXTENDS
HER NECK AND HER EYES,

622
00:23:10,227 --> 00:23:12,830
THERE'S TOO MUCH TENSION
CREATED IN HER FACE.

623
00:23:12,830 --> 00:23:14,998
I FEEL LIKE MARILYN.

624
00:23:14,998 --> 00:23:18,368
THE FIRST PHOTO SHOOT
I GOT "TOO PORN STAR,"

625
00:23:18,368 --> 00:23:20,871
SO THIS SHOOT, I JUST WANTED
TO MAKE SURE IT WAS

626
00:23:20,871 --> 00:23:23,841
MORE HIGH FASHION
AND NOT MORE SLUTTY.

627
00:23:27,177 --> 00:23:29,580
BRITTANY--SHE'S STILL
GETTING A LITTLE BIT OF THIS

628
00:23:29,580 --> 00:23:34,485
PORNO KIND-OF-MOVEMENT
THING GOING ON.

629
00:23:36,086 --> 00:23:37,855
LOOK AT THEM!

630
00:23:37,855 --> 00:23:40,457
THEY'RE SO CUTE!

631
00:23:40,457 --> 00:23:42,526
I'M GONNA NEED YOU
NOT TO SCRATCH THE FLEAS.

632
00:23:42,526 --> 00:23:44,061
COME ON, BABY,
PULL THOSE DOGS IN.

633
00:23:44,061 --> 00:23:46,597
THEY'RE RUNNING YOU.
YEAH. SEXY. GREAT.

634
00:23:46,597 --> 00:23:47,865
BRANDY LOOKED REALLY GREAT.

635
00:23:47,865 --> 00:23:50,868
I THINK THAT HER SHOT
WAS VERY DYNAMIC.

636
00:23:50,868 --> 00:23:54,037
WHOA!

637
00:23:54,037 --> 00:23:55,405
A LITTLE BIT TENSE.

638
00:23:55,405 --> 00:23:56,607
NO, NO, NO,
YOU WANT TO GO FORWARD.

639
00:23:56,607 --> 00:23:57,975
YOU DON'T WANT TO
LEAN BACK.

640
00:23:57,975 --> 00:24:00,344
YOUR EXPRESSION NEEDS TO ALTER
A LITTLE BIT.

641
00:24:00,344 --> 00:24:01,612
KEENYAH HAD
A BIT OF A STRUGGLE.

642
00:24:01,612 --> 00:24:05,082
SHE WAS UNABLE TO WORK THE DOG,
HER FACIAL EXPRESSION

643
00:24:05,082 --> 00:24:06,817
AND HER BODY.

644
00:24:06,817 --> 00:24:08,352
GO. STRONGER. TALLER.

645
00:24:08,352 --> 00:24:09,686
UP. UP, UP, UP, UP.

646
00:24:09,686 --> 00:24:11,021
THERE'S NO REASON WHY
YOUR LEGS HAVE TO BE PLANTED.

647
00:24:11,021 --> 00:24:12,022
IT'S NOT CEMENT.

648
00:24:12,022 --> 00:24:13,223
NAIMA WAS A LITTLE TOUGH.

649
00:24:13,223 --> 00:24:15,826
SHE DIDN'T SEEM TO COMMAND
HER EXPRESSIONS

650
00:24:15,826 --> 00:24:17,294
AS WELL AS SHE COULD HAVE.

651
00:24:17,294 --> 00:24:19,062
CHIN DOWN. STRAIGHTEN UP.

652
00:24:19,062 --> 00:24:20,764
SEXY. KEEP WORKING.

653
00:24:20,764 --> 00:24:21,932
GOOD! STRONG.

654
00:24:21,932 --> 00:24:23,667
TATIANA REALLY
IMPRESSED ME TODAY.

655
00:24:23,667 --> 00:24:27,037
SHE HANDLED THE DOGS
AND HERSELF AND THOSE FLOWERS.

656
00:24:27,037 --> 00:24:29,673
LAST NIGHT I GOT
A BUNCH OF STUFF OFF MY CHEST,

657
00:24:29,673 --> 00:24:31,508
AND I FEEL
SO MUCH BETTER NOW.

658
00:24:31,508 --> 00:24:34,344
HOPEFULLY IT HAS AN EFFECT
ON THE PHOTO SHOOT,

659
00:24:34,344 --> 00:24:36,213
AND THE JUDGES SEE
I'M MORE CONFIDENT.

660
00:24:36,213 --> 00:24:37,614
YOU LOOK GORGEOUS,
BY THE WAY.

661
00:24:37,614 --> 00:24:39,183
YEAH, THROW THAT HEAD BACK.

662
00:24:39,183 --> 00:24:40,184
KEEP MOVING.

663
00:24:40,184 --> 00:24:41,318
MICHELLE!

664
00:24:41,318 --> 00:24:43,453
DAMN, GIRL,
THAT'S THE WAY TO OWN A SET.

665
00:24:43,453 --> 00:24:45,155
MICHELLE WAS
A WONDERFUL MODEL.

666
00:24:45,155 --> 00:24:46,823
SHE IS INCREDIBLY
STATUESQUE.

667
00:24:46,823 --> 00:24:50,861
SHE'S GOT
WONDERFUL FEATURES.

668
00:24:50,861 --> 00:24:53,230
I LOVE IT. GORGEOUS.

669
00:24:53,230 --> 00:24:55,032
YOU OWNING IT, MAMA.

670
00:24:55,032 --> 00:24:57,501
LLUVY DOES NOT HAVE
A CONVENTIONAL SORT OF BEAUTY

671
00:24:57,501 --> 00:25:01,605
THAT THE OTHER GIRLS HAVE,
AND I LOVE HOW FOCUSED SHE WAS.

672
00:25:01,605 --> 00:25:05,008
TRY NOT TO HOLD THE FLOWERS
LIKE YOU'RE ON A PAGEANT.

673
00:25:05,008 --> 00:25:07,244
BECAUSE IT'S A LITTLE LIKE,
"HI, I WON MISS AMERICA."

674
00:25:07,244 --> 00:25:08,845
I DON'T FEEL
LIKE YOU'RE CONNECTING.

675
00:25:08,845 --> 00:25:10,113
THIS IS WHAT YOU LOOK LIKE--

676
00:25:10,113 --> 00:25:11,648
"(imitating drawl)
HI, I'M WALKING SOME DOGS."

677
00:25:11,648 --> 00:25:13,617
(normal voice)
SARAH IS ACTING LIKE
A PIECE OF DRIFTWOOD.

678
00:25:13,617 --> 00:25:15,085
SHE'S TOTALLY FORGETTING
THERE'S A HOT GUY

679
00:25:15,085 --> 00:25:16,186
STANDING OVER HER SHOULDER.

680
00:25:16,186 --> 00:25:17,621
CHIN DOWN. STRONGER!

681
00:25:17,621 --> 00:25:20,991
- I'M SORRY.
- THAT'S OKAY.

682
00:25:20,991 --> 00:25:22,226
NOELLE WENT AFTER ME.

683
00:25:22,226 --> 00:25:23,927
SHE SAID,
"WHAT SHOULD I EXPECT?"

684
00:25:23,927 --> 00:25:25,896
AND I WAS LIKE, "NOBODY TOLD ME
ANYTHING WHAT TO EXPECT."

685
00:25:25,896 --> 00:25:28,398
I'M NOT TELLING YOU ANYTHING
EITHER, I'M SORRY.

686
00:25:28,398 --> 00:25:29,633
IT'S A COMPETITION.

687
00:25:29,633 --> 00:25:30,867
CHIN DOWN. FACE OUT.

688
00:25:30,867 --> 00:25:32,035
LITTLE MORE FACE.

689
00:25:32,035 --> 00:25:33,604
I DON'T WANT TO SEE YOU
TRY AND MODEL.

690
00:25:33,604 --> 00:25:35,072
GOT IT.

691
00:25:35,072 --> 00:25:36,306
IT JUST LOOKS AWKWARD.

692
00:25:36,306 --> 00:25:38,675
NOELLE REALLY WANTED TO MAKE
THE PICTURE WORK.

693
00:25:38,675 --> 00:25:42,546
