IT WAS DIFFICULT THOUGH.

694
00:25:42,546 --> 00:25:45,082
GIRL, COME ON,
I GOT THAT ONE, KEEP MOVING IT.

695
00:25:45,082 --> 00:25:46,316
FLOWERS ARE LOOKING
A LITTLE FUNNY,

696
00:25:46,316 --> 00:25:47,384
LIKE YOU'VE GOT A BAGUETTE.

697
00:25:47,384 --> 00:25:48,518
LOOK AT ME, KAHLEN.

698
00:25:48,518 --> 00:25:50,387
KAHLEN, WORKING
WITH THE DOGS AND FLOWERS--

699
00:25:50,387 --> 00:25:52,055
SHE KEPT POPPING OUT
HER BUTT.

700
00:25:52,055 --> 00:25:53,457
I WANT YOU TO FEEL THE GUY
CHECKING YOU OUT

701
00:25:53,457 --> 00:25:54,491
OVER YOUR SHOULDER.

702
00:25:54,491 --> 00:25:55,492
YOU'VE GOT THE FLOWERS
IN THE HAND,

703
00:25:55,492 --> 00:25:56,660
THE DOG IN THE OTHER.

704
00:25:56,660 --> 00:25:58,629
SO I NEED YOU TO GET
INTO THE ROLE FOR ME.

705
00:25:58,629 --> 00:25:59,863
THAT'S YOUR INTERNAL
DIALOGUE.

706
00:25:59,863 --> 00:26:02,366
I THINK I CAN DO THIS.

707
00:26:02,366 --> 00:26:04,034
STOP LOOKING SO NICE.

708
00:26:04,034 --> 00:26:05,335
YEAH, WORK THAT.

709
00:26:05,335 --> 00:26:06,903
STRONG, STRAIGHT UP.

710
00:26:06,903 --> 00:26:09,406
YEAH, YOU'RE MY NEW GIRL,
COME ON.

711
00:26:09,406 --> 00:26:12,075
REBECCA COMES OUT
WITH HER PREPPY LITTLE LOOK,

712
00:26:12,075 --> 00:26:13,944
AND THEN SHE TURNS IT OUT
AND LOOKED INCREDIBLE

713
00:26:13,944 --> 00:26:15,579
IN THE CAMERA.

714
00:26:15,579 --> 00:26:17,714
THERE WAS QUITE A FEW GIRLS
AT MY SHOOT.

715
00:26:17,714 --> 00:26:19,816
IT'S THE MOST PRESSURE
I'VE EVER FELT,

716
00:26:19,816 --> 00:26:21,285
BUT I'M HERE FOR A REASON.

717
00:26:21,285 --> 00:26:22,519
I'M HERE TO WIN.

718
00:26:22,519 --> 00:26:23,820
ALL RIGHT. YEAH!

719
00:26:23,820 --> 00:26:25,589
YOU'RE MY NEW GIRL.

720
00:26:25,589 --> 00:26:28,759
I LOVE IT!

721
00:26:28,759 --> 00:26:31,228
♪♪♪

722
00:26:31,228 --> 00:26:33,196
- WE GOT TYRA MAIL!
- THERE'S TYRA MAIL.

723
00:26:33,196 --> 00:26:35,198
"TOMORROW YOU MEET
WITH THE JUDGES.

724
00:26:35,198 --> 00:26:37,200
ONLY 12 OF YOU WILL CONTINUE
IN THE HOPES OF BECOMING

725
00:26:37,200 --> 00:26:41,104
'AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.'
ONE OF YOU WILL BE ELIMINATED."

726
00:26:41,104 --> 00:26:44,174
I'M NOT LOOKING AT THAT
RIGHT NOW.

727
00:26:44,174 --> 00:26:46,143
EVERYBODY IS A LITTLE MORE
NERVOUS THIS TIME.

728
00:26:46,143 --> 00:26:47,177
I'M NOT GOING TO
SUGARCOAT IT.

729
00:26:47,177 --> 00:26:49,146
IF THEY'RE STILL
JUST GOING ON PHOTOS,

730
00:26:49,146 --> 00:26:50,614
THEN I THINK I'LL DO FINE.

731
00:26:50,614 --> 00:26:52,716
BUT IF WALKING COMPETITIONS,
HAVE ANYTHING TO DO WITH IT,

732
00:26:52,716 --> 00:26:56,620
THEN IT'S NOT LOOKING
TOO GOOD FOR ME.

733
00:26:56,620 --> 00:27:00,590
♪♪♪

734
00:27:00,590 --> 00:27:02,759
THAT'S A LOT BETTER,
THAT'S A LOT BETTER.

735
00:27:02,759 --> 00:27:03,927
SLOWING IT DOWN
HELPS YOU A LOT.

736
00:27:03,927 --> 00:27:06,096
I HONESTLY DON'T KNOW
WHAT IS GONNA HAPPEN

737
00:27:06,096 --> 00:27:07,364
AT ELIMINATION.

738
00:27:07,364 --> 00:27:09,866
I AM CONFIDENT IN MYSELF,
BUT I WISH I KNEW

739
00:27:09,866 --> 00:27:11,201
WHO WAS GOING HOME.

740
00:27:11,201 --> 00:27:13,470
BUT I DON'T, SO IT MAKES IT
JUST SO TOUGH TO WALK

741
00:27:13,470 --> 00:27:15,505
INTO THAT ROOM.

742
00:27:15,505 --> 00:27:18,442
♪♪♪

743
00:27:22,579 --> 00:27:25,282
IT IS TIME TO MAKE
OUR SECOND CUT,

744
00:27:25,282 --> 00:27:27,751
WHICH WILL BRING US
ONE STEP CLOSER TOWARDS

745
00:27:27,751 --> 00:27:30,287
DETERMINING WHO WILL BECOME
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

746
00:27:30,287 --> 00:27:32,823
WE HAVE SOME FABULOUS PRIZES--
A CONTRACT

747
00:27:32,823 --> 00:27:35,959
WITH TOP INTERNATIONAL MODELING
MANAGEMENT COMPANY FORD MODELS,

748
00:27:35,959 --> 00:27:38,462
A SPREAD IN "ELLE" MAGAZINE
SHOT BY WORLD-RENOWNED

749
00:27:38,462 --> 00:27:44,301
PHOTOGRAPHER GILLES BENSIMON
AND A $100,000 CONTRACT

750
00:27:44,301 --> 00:27:47,037
WITH COVER GIRL COSMETICS.

751
00:27:47,037 --> 00:27:49,539
WE HAVE SOME VERY OPINIONATED
JUDGES, STARTING WITH

752
00:27:49,539 --> 00:27:51,742
THE MOST OPINIONATED ONE,
MISS JANICE DICKINSON,

753
00:27:51,742 --> 00:27:53,744
ONE OF THE WORLD'S
FIRST SUPERMODELS.

754
00:27:53,744 --> 00:27:55,879
NIGEL BARKER,
A NOTED FASHION PHOTOGRAPHER.

755
00:27:55,879 --> 00:27:57,147
Hi, LADIES.

756
00:27:57,147 --> 00:28:00,183
NOLE MARIN, A PROMINENT
FASHION EDITOR AND STYLIST.

757
00:28:00,183 --> 00:28:01,184
HELLO, LADIES.

758
00:28:01,184 --> 00:28:02,185
IN PERSON, MIMI'S HERE.

759
00:28:02,185 --> 00:28:03,353
HI, MIMI!

760
00:28:03,353 --> 00:28:05,355
AND OUR SPECIAL GUEST JUDGE
SANDI BASS.

761
00:28:05,355 --> 00:28:06,656
HELLO, LADIES.

762
00:28:06,656 --> 00:28:07,924
HI. HI, SANDI.

763
00:28:07,924 --> 00:28:11,094
SANDI IS THE MUSE OF GIVENCHY
AND A MODEL SCOUT.

764
00:28:11,094 --> 00:28:13,096
THIS WEEK,
YOU'RE GONNA BE EVALUATED

765
00:28:13,096 --> 00:28:16,032
ON WHAT MISS J. TAUGHT YOU
ABOUT FIERCE RUNWAY WALKING.

766
00:28:16,032 --> 00:28:18,869
YOU WILL BE GIVEN THIS...

767
00:28:18,869 --> 00:28:23,006
50-CENT POTATO SACK,
AND IT IS UP TO YOU

768
00:28:23,006 --> 00:28:28,912
TO MAKE THIS POTATO SACK LOOK
LIKE A $20,000 COUTURE GOWN.

769
00:28:28,912 --> 00:28:33,383
AND, REBECCA,
YOU ARE FIRST, DARLING.

770
00:28:33,383 --> 00:28:37,821
♪♪♪

771
00:28:37,821 --> 00:28:42,626
WORK IT OUT.

772
00:28:42,626 --> 00:28:46,430
OH, SORRY.

773
00:29:01,878 --> 00:29:04,147
LOOK, GOT MY NEW SHOES ON.

774
00:29:04,147 --> 00:29:07,384
JUST WALK, SARAH.

775
00:29:31,408 --> 00:29:34,611
(laughing)
GO, GIRL!

776
00:29:34,611 --> 00:29:35,745
YEAH, SHE MADE IT.

777
00:29:37,747 --> 00:29:40,383
ALL RIGHTY.
FIRST IS REBECCA.

778
00:29:40,383 --> 00:29:44,254
I THOUGHT THAT YOUR WALK
WAS, YOU KNOW, GOOD,

779
00:29:44,254 --> 00:29:45,622
CONFIDENT, STRONG.

780
00:29:45,622 --> 00:29:49,092
I THINK YOU KIND OF FORGOT
WHAT TYRA'S DIRECTIONS WERE.

781
00:29:49,092 --> 00:29:50,193
IT DIDN'T LOOK EXPENSIVE.

782
00:29:50,193 --> 00:29:51,895
IT READ BURLAP TO ME.

783
00:29:51,895 --> 00:29:54,397
YOU HAD A PHOTO
IN GRIFFITH PARK,

784
00:29:54,397 --> 00:29:58,268
AND YOU HAD TO SELL FLOWERS,
AND YOU HAD TO HANDLE TEN DOGS.

785
00:29:58,268 --> 00:29:59,636
HERE'S YOUR BEST SHOT.

786
00:29:59,636 --> 00:30:00,937
OH, CUTE, CUTE, CUTE.

787
00:30:00,937 --> 00:30:02,939
OVERALL, I THINK IT'S
A GREAT, GREAT SHOT.

788
00:30:02,939 --> 00:30:04,941
THE DOGS LOOK GREAT,
YOU LOOK GREAT.

789
00:30:04,941 --> 00:30:06,943
KIND OF LOOKS, LIKE,
A LITTLE SLUTTY THOUGH,

790
00:30:06,943 --> 00:30:08,912
LIKE, REAL '40s PINUP,
I'M DIGGING IT.

791
00:30:08,912 --> 00:30:12,349
I THINK YOU HAVE EVERYTHING
TOGETHER FOR A MODEL.

792
00:30:12,349 --> 00:30:13,617
YOU NEED TO WORK
ON YOUR PRESENCE.

793
00:30:13,617 --> 00:30:17,120
I DIDN'T FEEL
THAT YOU EMBRA--

794
00:30:17,120 --> 00:30:18,788
OH, MY GOD!

795
00:30:18,788 --> 00:30:20,457
SHE JUST--

796
00:30:20,457 --> 00:30:21,591
CAN SOMEBODY
CALL THE PARAMEDICS?

797
00:30:21,591 --> 00:30:23,360
CALL THE POLICE!

798
00:30:28,031 --> 00:30:30,367
YOU HAD A PHOTO
IN GRIFFITH PARK.

799
00:30:30,367 --> 00:30:31,935
HERE'S YOUR BEST SHOT.

800
00:30:31,935 --> 00:30:33,136
WOW, CUTE, CUTE, CUTE!

801
00:30:33,136 --> 00:30:35,138
KIND OF LOOKS,
LIKE, A LITTLE SLUTTY THOUGH.

802
00:30:35,138 --> 00:30:37,140
YOU NEED TO WORK
ON YOUR PRESENCE.

803
00:30:37,140 --> 00:30:40,777
I DIDN'T FEEL THAT YOU EMBRA--
OH, MY GOD!

804
00:30:40,777 --> 00:30:42,746
(gasps)
OH, MY GOD!

805
00:30:42,746 --> 00:30:44,080
SHE'S OUT OF IT.

806
00:30:44,080 --> 00:30:45,081
SOMEBODY CALL
THE PARAMEDICS.

807
00:30:45,081 --> 00:30:46,082
I'M CALLING 911.

808
00:30:46,082 --> 00:30:47,083
SHE JUST NEEDS HER...

809
00:30:47,083 --> 00:30:50,720
(gasps)
OKAY, SHE'S BLINKING.

810
00:30:50,720 --> 00:30:52,522
SHE'S OKAY.

811
00:30:52,522 --> 00:30:54,524
WHEN SOMETHING
LIKE THIS HAPPENS,

812
00:30:54,524 --> 00:30:56,526
YOU CAN'T BELIEVE
IT JUST HAPPENED.

813
00:30:56,526 --> 00:30:58,828
I MEAN, BECCA--
SHE'S EXPLAINED TO ME

814
00:30:58,828 --> 00:31:00,830
THAT SHE HAS
A PREEXISTING CONDITION

815
00:31:00,830 --> 00:31:02,098
WHERE SHE COLLAPSES.

816
00:31:02,098 --> 00:31:04,100
SHE HAS HAD TESTS DONE
SINCE SHE WAS 3 YEARS OLD,

817
00:31:04,100 --> 00:31:09,239
BUT IT'S BEEN SIX OR SEVEN YEARS
SINCE HER LAST COLLAPSE.

818
00:31:14,544 --> 00:31:16,780
HOW MANY PEOPLE
WERE SCARED?

819
00:31:16,780 --> 00:31:17,781
ME TOO.

820
00:31:17,781 --> 00:31:19,015
I WAS REALLY,
REALLY SCARED.

821
00:31:19,015 --> 00:31:21,017
THE PARAMEDICS--
THEY TOOK REBECCA

822
00:31:21,017 --> 00:31:23,186
TO THE HOSPITAL,
AND SHE'S OKAY.

823
00:31:23,186 --> 00:31:25,188
SO WE'RE GOING TO CONTINUE
CONTINUE WITH JUDGING,

824
00:31:25,188 --> 00:31:27,357
IF THAT'S OKAY
WITH EVERYBODY.

825
00:31:27,357 --> 00:31:29,459
OKAY, SO, EVERYBODY,
JUST TAKE A... (inhales)

826
00:31:29,459 --> 00:31:31,461
(exhales)

827
00:31:31,461 --> 00:31:35,165
WE ARE GOING TO RESUME
WITH TATIANA.

828
00:31:35,165 --> 00:31:37,167
SO YOU HAD TO WORK
A BROWN POTATO SACK

829
00:31:37,167 --> 00:31:40,770
LIKE IT WAS
A $20,000 COUTURE GOWN.

830
00:31:40,770 --> 00:31:43,106
YOU WERE WALKING LIKE
EACH FOOT WEIGHS A TON.

831
00:31:43,106 --> 00:31:45,008
BE LIGHT ON YOUR FEET.

832
00:31:45,008 --> 00:31:47,410
YOU HAD A PHOTO SHOOT
IN GRIFFITH PARK, AND YOU HAD

833
00:31:47,410 --> 00:31:50,747
TO CONTROL FLOWERS,
A FINE MAN IN THE BACKGROUND

834
00:31:50,747 --> 00:31:52,649
AND TEN DOGS.

835
00:31:52,649 --> 00:31:53,650
BEAUTIFUL.

836
00:31:53,650 --> 00:31:54,651
GORGEOUS FACE.

837
00:31:54,651 --> 00:31:55,752
ABSOLUTELY GORGEOUS.

838
00:31:55,752 --> 00:31:57,454
STEPHANIE SEYMOUR
MEETS JACQUELINE BISSET.

839
00:31:57,454 --> 00:31:58,455
WONDERFUL.

840
00:31:58,455 --> 00:31:58,922
THANK YOU.

841
00:31:58,922 --> 00:31:59,923
NEXT WE HAVE TIFFANY.

842
00:31:59,923 --> 00:32:01,925
WHEN YOU WERE GOING
DOWN THE STAIRS,

843
00:32:01,925 --> 00:32:04,060
IT LOOKED LIKE YOU NEEDED
A CANE OR A WALKER.

844
00:32:04,060 --> 00:32:07,130
YOU'VE GOT TO DO STAIRMASTER
WITH YOUR HEELS ON.

845
00:32:07,130 --> 00:32:08,231
WOW, GOOD CONFIDENCE.

846
00:32:08,231 --> 00:32:09,332
CLOSE UP, PLEASE.

847
00:32:09,332 --> 00:32:10,700
OOH.

848
00:32:10,700 --> 00:32:13,069
A LITTLE CHEROKEE INDIAN,
A LITTLE BLACK GIRL,

849
00:32:13,069 --> 00:32:15,071
A LITTLE CHINESE GIRL,
A LITTLE SPANISH GIRL...

850
00:32:15,071 --> 00:32:16,072
THE EYES ARE BEAUTIFUL.

851
00:32:16,072 --> 00:32:17,073
I'M LOVING IT.

852
00:32:17,073 --> 00:32:18,074
SARAH.

853
00:32:18,074 --> 00:32:20,076
I'M SORRY,
BUT YOU WERE WALKING

854
00:32:20,076 --> 00:32:21,077
LIKE THE FUNKY CHICKEN.

855
00:32:21,077 --> 00:32:22,212
YOUR HEAD KEPT BOBBING.

856
00:32:22,212 --> 00:32:23,947
YOU ARE NOT A FASHION MODEL
ON THE RUNWAY.

857
00:32:23,947 --> 00:32:25,048
YOU HAD SUCH NERVOUS ENERGY.

858
00:32:25,048 --> 00:32:28,051
I SAW EVERY "OH, MY GOD"
ALL OVER YOUR FACE

859
00:32:28,051 --> 00:32:29,052
AND ALL OVER YOUR BODY.

860
00:32:29,052 --> 00:32:30,487
HERE IS YOUR BEST SHOT.

861
00:32:30,487 --> 00:32:32,489
IT'S NOT POUNCING OUT
AT ME ENOUGH.

862
00:32:32,489 --> 00:32:33,790
HER BODY ISN'T STRONG.

863
00:32:33,790 --> 00:32:36,059
I DON'T FEEL THE CONFIDENCE
IN THE OVERALL PHOTO.

864
00:32:36,059 --> 00:32:37,060
CAN WE SEE A CLOSE-UP?

865
00:32:37,060 --> 00:32:38,328
- FACE IS BEAUTIFUL.
- YEAH.

866
00:32:38,328 --> 00:32:40,964
YOU HAVE THAT VERY
OLD-FASHIONED KIND OF BEAUTY.

867
00:32:40,964 --> 00:32:43,867
- SHE DOES.
- NEXT WE HAVE LLUVY.

868
00:32:43,867 --> 00:32:45,869
YOU WERE THE ONLY GIRL
THAT DID SOMETHING

869
00:32:45,869 --> 00:32:47,170
WITH THAT SACK.

870
00:32:47,170 --> 00:32:49,406
TO ME IT WASN'T A SACK ANYMORE,
IT WAS A DRESS.

871
00:32:49,406 --> 00:32:51,408
I WAS LIKE,
"OOH, I WANT TO BUY THAT."

872
00:32:51,408 --> 00:32:53,176
I THOUGHT YOU WERE GIVING
MORE OF A SEXY CHIHUAHUA WALK

873
00:32:53,176 --> 00:32:55,211
THAN A REAL FASHION WALK.

874
00:32:55,211 --> 00:32:56,813
YOUR PERSONALITY IS
IMPORTANT, BUT DON'T LET IT

875
00:32:56,813 --> 00:32:59,749
OVERSHADOW WHAT YOU HAVE ON.

876
00:32:59,749 --> 00:33:00,817
GORGEOUS!

877
00:33:00,817 --> 00:33:01,918
YEAH. LOOKS FIERCE.

878
00:33:01,918 --> 00:33:02,986
ALL RIGHT, LLUVY. THANK YOU.

879
00:33:02,986 --> 00:33:04,354
MICHELLE.

880
00:33:04,354 --> 00:33:07,724
THERE WAS NOTHING POSITIVE
ABOUT THAT WALK WHATSOEVER.

881
00:33:07,724 --> 00:33:09,826
TO ME, YOU LOOKED LIKE
YOU'RE MODELING FOR THE FARMERS

882
00:33:09,826 --> 00:33:11,861
IN THE POTATO FACTORY--
LIKE, "HERE'S THE NEW SACK!

883
00:33:11,861 --> 00:33:12,862
Y'ALL WANT THIS.

884
00:33:12,862 --> 00:33:14,831
THESE HOLD 50 POTATOES."

885
00:33:14,831 --> 00:33:15,832
FIERCE.

886
00:33:15,832 --> 00:33:17,834
- WOW.
- LOOK AT THAT EYE.

887
00:33:17,834 --> 00:33:19,703
IT'S, LIKE, ON THE SIDE
OF YOUR HEAD LIKE AN ANTELOPE.

888
00:33:19,703 --> 00:33:20,837
I KNOW THAT SOUNDS
LIKE AN INSULT,

889
00:33:20,837 --> 00:33:22,972
BUT NO, THAT IS AMAZING.
THAT'S WHAT MODELS ARE.

890
00:33:22,972 --> 00:33:24,207
MODELS ARE WEIRD.

891
00:33:24,207 --> 00:33:25,608
THEY'RE DIFFERENT,
AND THAT'S WHAT MAKES THAT PHOTO

892
00:33:25,608 --> 00:33:28,111
SO AMAZINGLY GORGEOUS.

893
00:33:28,111 --> 00:33:29,679
BRANDY.

894
00:33:29,679 --> 00:33:31,681
I THOUGHT YOU MIGHT COME DOWN
THE END OF THE RUNWAY

895
00:33:31,681 --> 00:33:33,483
AND ACTUALLY SMACK ME
IN THE FACE.

896
00:33:33,483 --> 00:33:34,184
YOU LOOK PISSED OFF.

897
00:33:34,184 --> 00:33:37,620
THERE'S A MODEL ANGRY,
AND THERE'S A...

898
00:33:37,620 --> 00:33:39,255
YOU HAD THAT KIND OF...
(grunts)

899
00:33:39,255 --> 00:33:40,290
YOU ANGRY, GIRL.

900
00:33:40,290 --> 00:33:41,458
HERE IS YOUR BEST SHOT.

901
00:33:41,458 --> 00:33:42,692
- YES.
- OOH.

902
00:33:42,692 --> 00:33:44,094
THE OVERALL SHAPE
OF THE FACE IS BEAUTIFUL...

903
00:33:44,094 --> 00:33:45,328
GORGEOUS.

904
00:33:45,328 --> 00:33:46,730
- BUT THERE'S SOMETHING--
- THERE'S NO PASSION

905
00:33:46,730 --> 00:33:48,198
IN THE EYES,
I DON'T THINK.

906
00:33:48,198 --> 00:33:50,100
CHRISTINA.

907
00:33:50,100 --> 00:33:51,801
YOUR HAIR GOT CAUGHT
ON YOUR LIP,

908
00:33:51,801 --> 00:33:53,103
AND YOU LEFT IT THERE.

909
00:33:53,103 --> 00:33:55,105
SOMETHING GETS CAUGHT,
AS A MODEL, YOU GO, LIKE...

910
00:33:55,105 --> 00:33:56,172
AND JUST KEEP IT GOING.

911
00:33:56,172 --> 00:33:57,373
WORK IT, LIKE,
"I KNEW IT WAS THERE."

912
00:33:57,373 --> 00:33:58,708
WORK IT OUT,
THAT'S IT, GIRL.

913
00:33:58,708 --> 00:33:59,843
HERE'S YOUR BEST SHOT.

914
00:33:59,843 --> 00:34:01,778
- THE FACE IS BORING.
- IT'S NOT BORING.

915
00:34:01,778 --> 00:34:04,681
YOU'RE QUITE BEAUTIFUL,
BUT YOU'RE NOT BRINGING IT

916
00:34:04,681 --> 00:34:05,682
FROM WITHIN.

917
00:34:05,682 --> 00:34:07,717
NAIMA.

918
00:34:07,717 --> 00:34:08,718
WORK ON YOUR TURN.

919
00:34:08,718 --> 00:34:10,186
THANK YOU. VERY WEIRD.

920
00:34:10,186 --> 00:34:12,222
YOU'RE GONNA KNOCK
OTHER MODELS LIKE SKITTLES

921
00:34:12,222 --> 00:34:14,124
ACROSS THE RUNWAY
